<svg
  class="blog-diagram"
  width="800"
  height="366"
  viewBox="0 0 800 366"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  role="img"
  aria-labelledby="gmBoundaryTitle gmBoundaryDesc"
>
  <title id="gmBoundaryTitle">Where companies draw the GM boundary</title>
  <desc id="gmBoundaryDesc">Five ways companies draw the general manager boundary: geography at DoorDash, Uber, and Caviar, category at Amazon and Walmart, business line at Robinhood, customer segment at Intuit, and function at Apple, which deliberately has no GMs.</desc>

  <text class="head" x="60" y="48">Boundary</text>
  <text class="head" x="225" y="48">Example</text>
  <text class="head" x="390" y="48">What it means</text>

  <line class="rule-strong" x1="60" y1="60" x2="780" y2="60" />

  <text class="boundary" x="60" y="94">Geography</text>
  <text class="company" x="225" y="94">DoorDash · Uber · Caviar</text>
  <text class="what" x="390" y="94">One city, one owner: growth, ops, supply, service quality</text>
  <line class="rule-light" x1="60" y1="118" x2="780" y2="118" />

  <text class="boundary" x="60" y="152">Category</text>
  <text class="company" x="225" y="152">Amazon · Walmart</text>
  <text class="what" x="390" y="152">Selection, pricing, inventory, promotion in one model</text>
  <line class="rule-light" x1="60" y1="176" x2="780" y2="176" />

  <text class="boundary" x="60" y="210">Business line</text>
  <text class="company" x="225" y="210">Robinhood</text>
  <text class="what" x="390" y="210">Product teams inside Brokerage, Crypto, Say, and Cash</text>
  <line class="rule-light" x1="60" y1="234" x2="780" y2="234" />

  <text class="boundary" x="60" y="268">Segment</text>
  <text class="company" x="225" y="268">Intuit</text>
  <text class="what" x="390" y="268">Consumer, small business and mid-market, and services</text>
  <line class="rule-light" x1="60" y1="292" x2="780" y2="292" />

  <text class="boundary boundary-alt" x="60" y="326">Function</text>
  <text class="company company-alt" x="225" y="326">Apple</text>
  <text class="what what-alt" x="390" y="326">No GMs by design: one P&amp;L, integration lives in the functions</text>
  <line class="rule-strong" x1="60" y1="350" x2="780" y2="350" />
</svg>

<style>
  .blog-diagram {
    --counterexample: #b42318;
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  .rule-strong {
    stroke: var(--color-text-muted);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .rule-light {
    stroke: var(--color-border);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .head {
    fill: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .boundary {
    fill: var(--color-text);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .company {
    fill: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .what {
    fill: var(--color-text);
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .boundary-alt,
  .company-alt,
  .what-alt {
    fill: var(--counterexample);
  }

  .what-alt {
    font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
